[size=5][b]Description[/b][/size]
A save editor for [b]MechWarrior 5: Clans[/b], built from scratch around three ideas: never risk your saves, do in one click what used to take fifty, and look like it belongs in the game.

The same download also edits [b]MechWarrior 5: Mercenaries[/b] saves ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mechwarrior5mercenaries/mods/1666]Mercenaries page[/url]): switch games with the tabs at the top, and each keeps its own open save.

[size=5][b]Links[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]MechWarrior 5: Mercenaries:[/b] the same download, on its [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mechwarrior5mercenaries/mods/1666]MechWarrior 5: Mercenaries page[/url]
[*][b]Documentation:[/b] [url=https://mindattic.github.io/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/]mindattic.github.io/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor[/url] ([url=https://mindattic.github.io/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/docs/USER_GUIDE.html]user guide[/url])
[*][b]Source code:[/b] [url=https://github.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor]github.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor[/url] (issues and feedback welcome)
[/list]

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[b]Pick saves by name, not by GUID[/b]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/main/assets/clans-01-campaigns.png[/img]
Every save is listed by its load-menu name, with campaign, date and Kerenskies; autosaves are marked. Double-click to open.

[b]Resources: Kerenskies, Honor, salvage, crew, MXP[/b]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/main/assets/clans-02-resources.png[/img]
Set Kerenskies, Merits and Honor (Honor also moves the Honor level track), mech, weapon and equipment components, technicians (and the mech bay's technician pool), scientists, crew upgrades, and per-chassis mech experience. Quick +10 / +100 / +1K buttons on every value.

[b]Mechs: your whole Touman at a glance[/b]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/main/assets/clans-03-mechs.png[/img]
Every 'Mech with its Sarna.net art, variant, tonnage, installed gear and condition.

[b]Repair, duplicate, rename[/b]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/main/assets/clans-04-mechs-damaged-selected.png[/img]
Tick 'Mechs (Shift+click, Select all, or [b]Select damaged[/b]) and [b]repair[/b] armor, every installed part and destroyed body parts, [b]duplicate[/b] them with the same loadout, fully repaired, or [b]rename[/b] them. Each 'Mech's mech bay plan follows it: copies get their own, and renames and removals carry over.

[b]Find and copy any 'Mech you own[/b]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/main/assets/clans-05-mechs-duplicate.png[/img]
Filter by name, chassis, variant or weapon. [b]Remove[/b] 'Mechs you don't want; any deployed in your Star or in the mech bay's work queue are kept.

[b]Weapons and equipment[/b]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/main/assets/clans-06-inventory.png[/img]
Edit your stock, requisition any weapon or piece of equipment seen in Clans campaigns, and add to or remove ticked items in bulk.

[b]Campaign progress[/b]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/main/assets/clans-07-progress.png[/img]
Honor level and experience, cycles elapsed, the technician pool, the research queue and completed research.

[b]One look per game: Clans ice and Mercs amber[/b]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mindattic/Mods.MechWarrior5.SaveEditor/main/assets/nexus/06-two-themes-mercs-amber-clans-ice.png[/img]
A cold steel and ice-cyan look for Clans and a gunmetal and amber look for Mercenaries, modeled on the games' own menus; it follows the game tab. Batch buttons stay greyed out until something is ticked, so an action only touches what you see. Six languages: English, Deutsch, Español, Français, 日本語, Русский.

[size=5][b]Your saves are safe[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]An original game save is [b]never overwritten[/b]. Saving writes a new save beside it and adds it to the game's load menu under the name you choose. The original stays byte-for-byte identical.
[*]Saves the editor writes carry a small, harmless marker the game ignores. Only those are ever updated in place, and the previous version is kept as a [b].bak[/b].
[*][b]Lossless or nothing:[/b] if a save can't be reproduced exactly, the editor refuses to edit it instead of guessing.
[*]The game's save index files are backed up before every change.
[*]Tested end to end: an automated suite edits copies of real campaign saves for both games, reopens every written file and checks each change, and edited saves have been loaded and played in both games.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[b]This is a program you run, not a mod the game loads.[/b] The download is one [b]MW5SaveEditor.exe[/b] (no .NET install needed). The game never starts it and it adds nothing to the game: you run it yourself.

[b]With Vortex[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Click [b]Mod Manager Download[/b]. Vortex installs it like any mod; the game ignores it.
[*]Vortex doesn't start it for you. In Vortex's [b]Mods[/b] list, right-click [b]MW5 Save Editor[/b] and choose [b]Open in File Manager[/b].
[*]In that folder, double-click [b]MW5SaveEditor.exe[/b].
[/list]
Tip: to start it from Vortex next time, open the [b]Tools[/b] panel on Vortex's [b]Dashboard[/b], choose [b]Add Tool[/b] and point it at that MW5SaveEditor.exe. Or right-click the exe and send a shortcut to your Desktop.

[b]Manual[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Click [b]Manual Download[/b] and extract the archive anywhere, for example your Desktop.
[*]Double-click [b]MW5SaveEditor.exe[/b].
[/list]

[b]Using it[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Quit the game, or stay on its main menu, so the save you edit isn't in use.
[*]Run [b]MW5SaveEditor.exe[/b] and choose [b]MERCENARIES[/b] or [b]CLANS[/b] at the top. Your saves are listed by name; double-click one to open it.
[*]Make your changes, type a name for the edited save, and press [b]Save as new[/b] (Ctrl+S).
[*]In the game, load the save with that name. Your original save is still there, unchanged.
[/list]

[b]Uninstalling:[/b] remove it in Vortex, or delete the folder you extracted (your settings are the [b]settings.json[/b] beside the exe). The 'Mech picture cache lives in [b]%LOCALAPPDATA%\MechWarrior5SaveEditor[/b]; delete it too for a clean removal.

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]MechWarrior 5: Mercenaries and/or MechWarrior 5: Clans on Windows (Steam or Epic). Game Pass / Microsoft Store saves live elsewhere and are untested; use Open to pick them at your own risk.
[*]Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit. The download is self-contained.
[*]No DLC or other mods required. Back up a campaign you care about before editing it, as with any save editor.
[*]Internet access only for the 'Mech pictures (from Sarna.net, cached after the first view). Everything else works offline.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Shout outs[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]JJ[/b], whose [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mechwarrior5mercenaries/mods/1466]MW5 Merc Save Editor[/url] inspired this one's scope. No code from it is used; its game data catalogs (MIT) seed the Mercenaries 'Mech and item lists.
[*][b]wmtorode[/b], whose original MW5 Mercs Save Editor showed that editing these saves was possible in the first place.
[*][url=https://www.sarna.net]Sarna.net[/url], the BattleTech wiki, for the 'Mech artwork shown in the editor.
[*][b]Piranha Games[/b] for MechWarrior 5: Mercenaries and Clans.
[*]Code written with an AI model (Claude).
[/list]

